Vita: DuskAudioSystem output goes to SceAudioOut (platform/vita/audio) instead of
an SDL audio stream (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, "Audio": audio thread core, priority
and suspend under the port's control; no SDL_AudioSpec across the enum boundary).
Only the output side changes: under TARGET_VITA the stream open/close and the
SDL_PutAudioStreamData call; pause/resume go through two helpers that call the same
SDL functions as before on other targets. Rendering (RenderNewAudioFrame, the DSP,
the resampler and mixing) is unchanged, so what the game hears cannot change;
surround output modes render stereo because the Vita has stereo output only.

--- a/src/dusk/audio/DuskAudioSystem.cpp
+++ b/src/dusk/audio/DuskAudioSystem.cpp
@@ -10,7 +10,14 @@
 #include "JSystem/JAudio2/JASDSPChannel.h"
 #include "JSystem/JAudio2/JASHeapCtrl.h"
 
+#if TARGET_VITA
+// The Vita sends the DSP output to SceAudioOut (platform/vita/audio) instead of an SDL
+// audio stream: the same pull model, but the audio thread's core, priority and
+// suspend behavior belong to the port. Rendering below is unchanged.
+#include "audio/audio_out.hpp"
+#else
 #include <SDL3/SDL_init.h>
+#endif
 #include <tracy/Tracy.hpp>
 
